INTRODUCTION
------------

This release of the MTSX RSS provides dramatic performance improvements
over previous RSS releases by further utilizing the extended memory 
capability of the 386 and 486 PCs.  (All previous releases were limited
to the use of conventional memory for computational purposes.) To take
advantage of these performance enhancements your machine must be a 386
(or 486) based machine with 4M of memory (1M lower + 3M or more 
extended). Otherwise the application will only use conventional memory
(640K), and the performance will be only slightly faster than  previous 
releases.  This application is compatible with DOS 6.0,  but cannot be
ran as a Double Space file. 

With extended memory, the application will now run with less than 200K
of conventional memory available!  Resident programs and TSR (Terminate
& Stay Resident) utilities no longer have to be disabled.  This has 
also permitted the installation procedure to be significantly improved
and simplified.  The CONFIG.SYS modifications required to run the 
application have been automated, and are described in the rest of this
introduction.

A new Tutorial section (Chapter 3) has been added to the manual to 
discuss programming requirements of some of the specific MT2000, 
MTX8000, MTX9000, and MTS2000 models.  This release added support for 
Secure MTS2000 radio models, and also corrected defects in the 
previous release.

EXTENDED MEMORY OPERATION
-------------------------

Previous versions of this application recommended the use of extended
memory for a RAMDrive to reduce the disk I/O access time.  (The 
application however, only used conventional memory for actual 
execution.)  This version does not require the use of a RAMDrive or  
SMARTDrive.

The new installation program will determine if your system has an 
adequate amount of memory available (3Meg) and a 386 (or 486) CPU for 
extended memory operation. If present, the extended memory version of 
RSS will be installed, otherwise the conventional memory version will 
be installed. In the latter case, approximately 615K of available 
conventional memory must be available.

The installation will set Files = 30, add the HIMEM.SYS memory 
manager and EMM386.EXE memory manager to the CONFIG.SYS file.  If you 
had previously set up a RAMDrive,  you will be prompted to manually 
remove this command. The installation routine is unable to remove the 
RAMDrive statement from the CONFIG.SYS file.  Otherwise, the extended 
memory will not be available for the RSS application to use. The 
installation program will prompt before any CONFIG.SYS modifications, 
and will also create a backup copy of the original (OLDCON.FIG)

On some computers the installation routine may have difficulty updating
the CONFIG.SYS file. On COMPAQ portable computers EMM386.EXE is not 
used. In cases such as these the CONFIG.SYS file will have to be 
editted manually. Consult your DOS and PC manuals for information on 
how to configure extended memory.  

Note: The DOS MEM command may be used to determine the amount of 
available memory in your machine (i.e. type c:\dos\mem. The location 
of  MEM.EXE may differ on your machine.)   If the command reports 3000K
or more of available extended memory, you can take full advantage of 
these enhancements.

PERFORMANCE EXPECTATIONS
------------------------

The time required to calculate (validate) the codeplug data is highly 
dependent on:

1)      The type of PC used (386 or 486; 25 MHz, 33 MHz, 66 MHz, etc.)
2)      The amount and type of data to be validated.  

The time required to transfer the data to the radio (program) is only 
dependent on the amount of data (i.e. the radio model / configuration).
The following table shows the type of performance you should expect 
with this application:

		Validate / Program Time (Minutes)
		---------------------------------
 
		    Extended Memory     Non-Extended Memory
Model      Comment   386       486         386       486        
		   (25 MHz)  (66 MHz)    (25 MHz)  (66 MHz)
MT2000     Note 1    0.6       0.5         0.8       0.6
MT2000     Note 2    3.5       1.9         4.7       2.3
MTX8000    Note 3    0.7       0.6         0.9       0.6
MTS2000    Note 4    6.1       3.5        12.3       4.6


Note 1: 16 Conventional Channels, 1 Scan List
Note 2: 128 Conventional Channels, 10 Scan Lists
Note 3: 3 Systems, 6 Personalities, 6 Subfleets, 1 Scan List, 
	1 Call List, 1 Phone List
Note 4: 10 Systems, 30 Personalities, 150 Talkgroups, 10 Scan Lists, 
	30 Call Lists, 1 Phone List

All non-extended memory times are with a RAMDrive.


DEFECT FIXES / ENHANCEMENTS
---------------------------

The following features and defects were addressed in this release:

1.  Added support for Vehicle Adapter (JVA).
2.  Added support for Secure models.
3.  Call ID lists are limited to 6 characters on 6-digit display models.
4.  Bandwidth selection was added for UHF/VHF trunking systems.
5.  Allow selection of Supervisor Pool ID on Type I systems with 
    Unlimited Private Call.
6.  Allow capability to disable MDC emergency feature.
7.  Removed capability of adding an announcement talkgroup to the 
    Zone/Channel list when the announcement talkgroup is disabled in 
    the personality. 
8.  Random 'merge errors' with TCMS merge on Private Systems 
    models have been corrected. 
9.  Allowed capability of enabling dynamic regrouping modes on more then
    one trunking system. 
10. Corrected default value for transmit deviation when a receive 
    only conventional personality is changed to receive/transmit.
11. Corrected problem which caused a radio codeplug to be corrupted
    if print screen was pressed during programming. 
12. Added capability of selecting the Universal ID personality on a 
    system. NOTE: If you are using this new RSS to read existing 
    archives/radios and the Universal ID data had been previously altered, 
    verify the Universal ID data in the Personalities before programming.
13. Correct cloning problem on Private BN models, which prevents the 
    cloning of BN models to BN models due to 'feature mismatch error'.
14. Correct problem which prevents the selection of a newly created
    system on a newly created personality under certain conditions. 
15. Correct problem which causes 'Bad Block Type Error' on entry 
    of service mode before a radio or radio archive has been read. 
16. Allow Keypad Lock on three position toggle switch.
17. Remove TX Power Level fields on trunking and conventional 
    personalities for 800 and 900 MHz radio.  

RUNNING THE PROGRAM
-------------------

The installation process will install the program on a \mrss\mtsx 
sub-directory.   In addition, a batch file (MTSX.BAT) will be placed 
in your C: drive root directory.

To execute the application, type:  \MTSX.       

